Notebook[{
Cell["Lesson 3 log \[CenterDot] The transformer, part by part", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"0c71c726-2687-4583-9c1f-23aafccae78a"],

Cell["\<\
Written 2026-11-24 01:51 UTC by lesson3_transformer_parts.nb. 27 of 27 checks \
pass.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d6e40337-25cc-48f1-8a6a-08213b89a739"],

Cell["\<\
Paper: A. Vaswani et al., Attention Is All You Need, NeurIPS 2017, \
arXiv:1706.03762. Every part is coded from plain arrays and as a Wolfram net \
built from primitive layers, and the two are checked against each other. The \
trained demo net for this paper is in ref3_transformer_vaswani2017.nb; Lesson \
4 assembles these parts into a tensor-algebra transformer.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0a0db04e-57ea-4b3c-a30d-56fc28df69d4"],

Cell["1. Scaled dot-product attention", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c674bf78-6825-43f2-836a-68714b97b204"],

Cell["\<\
Each query is compared with every key by a dot product; the softmax of the \
scores gives weights that sum to 1, and the output is the weighted average of \
the values (Section 3.2.1).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2ebe2403-cafd-4fce-8ee3-54e193ed9e1a"],

Cell["Attention(Q, K, V) = softmax( Q K\[Transpose] / \[Sqrt]dk ) V", \
"Program",ExpressionUUID->"8218feef-3af9-435e-a524-c6277a558243"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["PASS  ",
  FontWeight->Bold,
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0.5, 0]],
 "the formula coded from arrays equals AttentionLayer[\"Dot\", \
\"ScoreRescaling\" -> \"DimensionSqrt\"] (4 queries, 7 keys)"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c0e35a6a-6f84-4ad8-8baf-8ba2b0dc5eee"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["PASS  ",
  FontWeight->Bold,
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0.5, 0]],
 "every row of attention weights sums to 1"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a08eeb75-479e-49a9-965c-a2318cb1d43b"],

Cell["2. Why the scores are divided by \[Sqrt]dk", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"fa8c1dba-03c8-4db6-8c7f-02b7578fc20b"],

Cell["\<\
If the components of q and k are independent with mean 0 and variance 1, \
their dot product has mean 0 and variance dk (footnote 4 of the paper). For \
dk = 64 the scores are then about \[PlusMinus]8, the softmax is close to \
one-hot, and its gradients are tiny. Dividing by \[Sqrt]dk brings the \
variance back to 1.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3df555eb-8522-40e6-b704-4b65a88f72ed"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {"\<\"\"\>", "\<\"variance of q\[CenterDot]k\"\>", "\<\"mean largest \
softmax weight (10 keys)\"\>"},
    {"\<\"unscaled\"\>", 
     TagBox[
      InterpretationBox[
       StyleBox["\<\"63.6\"\>",
        ShowStringCharacters->False],
       63.63034351331644,
       AutoDelete->True],
      NumberForm[#, 3]& ], 
     TagBox[
      InterpretationBox[
       StyleBox["\<\"0.868\"\>",
        ShowStringCharacters->False],
       0.8676329071218061,
       AutoDelete->True],
      NumberForm[#, 3]& ]},
    {"\<\"divided by \[Sqrt]64\"\>", 
     TagBox[
      InterpretationBox[
       StyleBox["\<\"0.994\"\>",
        ShowStringCharacters->False],
       0.9942241173955694,
       AutoDelete->True],
      NumberForm[#, 3]& ], 
     TagBox[
      InterpretationBox[
       StyleBox["\<\"0.318\"\>",
        ShowStringCharacters->False],
       0.3181238458665638,
       AutoDelete->True],
      NumberForm[#, 3]& ]}
   },
   AutoDelete->False,
   GridBoxBackground->{"Columns" -> {{None}}, "Rows" -> {
       GrayLevel[0.85]}},
   GridBoxFrame->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}],
  "Grid"]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"1b66dd2d-edcd-4a60-adfa-6baccfa610c0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["PASS  ",
  FontWeight->Bold,
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0.5, 0]],
 "the variance of q\[CenterDot]k is about dk = 64 (measured 63.6)"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cc30ec05-36f4-4ad5-bee3-4a4f00568564"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["PASS  ",
  FontWeight->Bold,
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0.5, 0]],
 "after dividing by \[Sqrt]dk it is about 1"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a63f1033-deb2-43e8-9efb-ee7c7a5755b3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["PASS  ",
  FontWeight->Bold,
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0.5, 0]],
 "unscaled, the softmax is nearly one-hot (largest weight 0.87); scaled it is \
not (0.32)"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"442eff13-be1c-4123-9b58-e0913745b1b6"],

Cell["3. Masks: padding and causal", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"bf915b6c-eee7-416a-a293-ccb99f5a15a2"],

Cell["\<\
A mask is added to the scores before the softmax: 0 where attention is \
allowed, a very large negative number where it is not, so those weights \
become 0. A padding mask hides the padding at the end of short sequences. A \
causal mask stops position i of the decoder from seeing positions after i, so \
that it cannot read the word it is asked to predict (Section 3.2.3).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4220b2f9-33bc-4c8c-9d90-32d3a50d0760"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  RowBox[{"(", "\[NoBreak]", GridBox[{
     {"0.`", "\<\"\[Minus]\[Infinity]\"\>", "\<\"\[Minus]\[Infinity]\"\>", \
"\<\"\[Minus]\[Infinity]\"\>", "\<\"\[Minus]\[Infinity]\"\>"},
     {"0.`", 
      "0.`", "\<\"\[Minus]\[Infinity]\"\>", "\<\"\[Minus]\[Infinity]\"\>", \
"\<\"\[Minus]\[Infinity]\"\>"},
     {"0.`", "0.`", 
      "0.`", "\<\"\[Minus]\[Infinity]\"\>", "\<\"\[Minus]\[Infinity]\"\>"},
     {"0.`", "0.`", "0.`", "0.`", "\<\"\[Minus]\[Infinity]\"\>"},
     {"0.`", "0.`", "0.`", "0.`", "0.`"}
    },
    GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Center}}, "Rows" -> {{Baseline}}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {
        Offset[0.27999999999999997`], {
         Offset[0.7]}, 
        Offset[0.27999999999999997`]}, "Rows" -> {
        Offset[0.2], {
         Offset[0.4]}, 
        Offset[0.2]}}], "\[NoBreak]", ")"}],
  Function[BoxForm`e$, 
   MatrixForm[BoxForm`e$]]]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"65e1bc4e-3f9f-460a-\
9233-9310697582b7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["PASS  ",
  FontWeight->Bold,
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0.5, 0]],
 "causal: changing positions 5 and 6 leaves outputs 1\[Ellipsis]4 unchanged"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"60237e47-d482-4220-a4c8-42598a02c28d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["PASS  ",
  FontWeight->Bold,
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0.5, 0]],
 "the causal mask coded from arrays equals AttentionLayer with \"Mask\" -> \
\"Causal\""
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"36b9538f-d9db-4797-ac51-17caeed51454"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["PASS  ",
  FontWeight->Bold,
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0.5, 0]],
 "padding: with 4 real keys, changing the 2 padding keys changes nothing"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f07eae9d-6a42-46f7-9592-663d64a77c45"],

Cell["\<\
In Wolfram, padding needs no mask: sequences of different lengths are \
\"Varying\" dimensions, and NetTrain pads and masks them itself.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7793ee59-ad94-4c2f-b318-d29748e9171d"],

Cell["4. Multi-head attention", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"d9a15cc2-2779-455d-9fc1-fe1b350381b8"],

Cell["\<\
One attention with dmodel-dimensional queries is replaced by h attentions \
with dk = dmodel/h dimensions each, on different learned projections; their \
outputs are joined and projected again. The total cost is about that of one \
full-size attention, but each head can attend to different things (Section \
3.2.2).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"01a62d45-de2e-401f-b8cd-cd501a2fff00"],

Cell["\<\
MultiHead(Q, K, V) = Concat(head_1, \[Ellipsis], head_h) W^O
head_i = Attention(Q W_i^Q, K W_i^K, V W_i^V)\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"f3abca33-501c-4290-aacb-10feb0c199b7"],

Cell["\<\
As a Wolfram net, built from primitive layers: LinearLayer for the \
projections (all heads at once), ReshapeLayer to split dmodel features into h \
groups of dk, AttentionLayer with \"MultiHead\" -> True for the h scaled \
dot-product attentions, FlattenLayer to join the heads, and a last \
LinearLayer for W^O.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"44d6c92b-e817-4e34-9a4a-c93ebb30fa56"],

