 StyleBox["PASS  ",
  FontWeight->Bold,
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0.5, 0]],
 "the smoothed loss is lowest when the model predicts the smoothed target, \
not when it is 99.9% sure"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"652df40e-71cc-42e2-98d3-452d7c7cd1d5"],

Cell["11. The warm-up learning-rate schedule", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"5fb5693c-65bc-480a-bdba-a00a4f530918"],

Cell["\<\
Adam with \[Beta]\:2081 = 0.9, \[Beta]\:2082 = 0.98, \[Epsilon] = 10\:207b\
\:2079. The rate rises linearly for the first 4000 steps, then falls as 1/\
\[Sqrt]step (Section 5.3). The warm-up protects the young network from large, \
badly-aimed steps.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3a8de5fb-a760-4670-a065-2ddb88e7ca87"],

Cell["\<\
lrate = dmodel^(\[Minus]0.5) \[CenterDot] min(step^(\[Minus]0.5), step \
\[CenterDot] warmup^(\[Minus]1.5)),     warmup = 4000\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"e584871f-780b-4a9b-a79a-5a29428026d8"],

